<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carloman I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 771</span> · Also known as Carloman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carloman I was a Frankish king, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a> and the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>, with whom he shared the kingdom from 768. Relations between the brothers were tense. Carloman's unexpected death in 771 allowed Charlemagne to seize his territories and unite the realm that became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carloman-i.jpg" alt="Carloman I" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: cgb.fr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denier_sous_Carloman_Ier.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
